					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "The PT4103 is a step-up DC/DC converter designed for driving up to 8 white LEDs in series from a single cell Lithium  Ion  battery  with  constant  current.  Because  it  directly regulates output current, the PT4103 is ideal for driving   light   emitting   diodes   (LEDs)   whose   light   intensity  is  proportional  to  the  current  passing  through  them,  not  the  voltage  across  their  terminals.  A  single  external  resistor  sets  LED  current  between  5mA  and  20mA, which can then be easily adjusted using either a DC voltage or a pulse width modulated (PWM) signal. Its  low  104mV  feedback  voltage  reduces  power  loss  and  improves  efficiency.  The  OV  pin  monitors  the  output   voltage   and   turns   off   the   converter   if   an   over-voltage condition is present due to an open circuit condition.   The   PT4103   is   available   in   SOT23-6      packages."
			(at 0 0 90)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "c9c7b6e8-cd4a-45b7-b5ac-547e455a6f43")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
